Report current, outdated, missing, foreign or unreadable skills. --agent optionally filters claude, codex, opencode, pi, omp, windsurf, cursor, gemini or antigravity; repeat it to select several.
--user is the default. Claude Code uses $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/skills or ~/.claude/skills; Antigravity uses ~/.gemini/config/skills; all other agents use ~/.agents/skills.
--project uses .claude/skills for Claude Code and .agents/skills otherwise, under the exact cwd without Git-root lookup or user overrides. The scope flags are mutually exclusive.
Shared paths reflect shared state, not separate copies. No hooks, settings, instruction files, credentials or network access; missing directories are not created.

Usage: agent-cli skill status

Flags:
      --agent <stringArray>  Select an agent; repeat to select several (default: all)
      --project              Use the native agent skill path under the exact current directory
      --user                 Use the agent's user skill location (default)
  -h, --help                 Print help
  -v, --verbose              Print diagnostic details to stderr

Examples:
  agent-cli skill status
  agent-cli skill status --project --agent claude --agent codex

Environment: CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR (Claude user scope only); system user home for --user
Exit codes: 0 reported, including missing or unreadable skills · 1 location or output failure · 2 usage error or unknown agent
